[1.167,"m","Deploy (--mode assisted): ov prints the commands and runs nothing"]
[1.167,"o","$ "]
[1.171,"o","ov stack deploy openvidu-e2e-gcp-el-s113145 --cloud gcp --gcp-project \"$GCP_PROJECT_ID\" --edition pro --openvidu-pro-license \"$OPENVIDU_PRO_LICENSE\" --deployment-type elastic --certificate-type selfsigned --param fixedNumberOfMediaNodes=1 --mode assisted\r\n"]
[6.171,"o","note: recorded this stack's infrastructure in openvidu-stack.yml, so the command that continues this deploy needs no flags\r\n"]
[6.171,"o","── PLAN · nothing below has run ───────────────────────────────────────\r\nRun these commands yourself in your Google Cloud project *** (region europe-west2, zone europe-west2-b); ov runs none of them:\r\n\r\n  # The template, rendered from the one embedded in this CLI for the elastic topology,\r\n  # and its variables, written out for you to read (the variables file is 0600: it\r\n  # carries the license):\r\n  #   .openvidu/gcp/tf-gpc-openvidu-pro-elastic.tf\r\n  #   .openvidu/gcp/openvidu.auto.tfvars.json\r\n  terraform -chdir=.openvidu/gcp init -input=false -no-color -force-copy\r\n  # If this stack already exists, read first what the apply would change: a new startup script\r\n  # (the domain, the certificate, the license, the Meet credentials or another OpenVidu CLI) REPLACES\r\n  # the machine that runs it, which starts again from scratch, and Terraform's plan says \"must be replaced\":\r\n  terraform -chdir=.openvidu/gcp plan\r\n  # Create the machines. deployedBy=instance: master-1 installs OpenVidu with the\r\n  # OpenVidu CLI and the other nodes join it. `apply` returns when Terraform is done (about 3 minutes, then OpenVidu installs).\r\n  terraform -chdir=.openvidu/gcp apply -auto-approve -input=false -no-color\r\n\r\n  # Read back where the stack is (sensitive outputs, such as a generated SSH key, show as\r\n  # <sensitive>: `terraform output -raw <name>` prints one).\r\n  terraform -chdir=.openvidu/gcp output\r\n  # What the stack published: URL, credentials and the stack's access, as Secret Manager secrets under the prefix the stack outputs (KUBECONFIG\r\n  # appears once OpenVidu is up: until then this read fails, and the command that continues the deploy waits for it).\r\n  PREFIX=\"$(terraform -chdir=.openvidu/gcp output -raw secret_prefix)\"\r\n  gcloud secrets versions access latest --secret=${PREFIX}KUBECONFIG --project=***\r\n\r\nNothing above has been run. Once these commands have finished, run this same command again:\r\n\r\n  ov stack deploy openvidu-e2e-gcp-el-s113145 --cloud gcp --mode assisted\r\n\r\nIt finds the machines, waits for OpenVidu to come up and registers this directory as the\r\nstack. It creates nothing in your account.\r\n── end of plan ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n"]
